# [DD-13b.W23.3] `under`'s duplicate refusal — the other half of
# `under_key_distinct.rxtin`, and neither is an instrument without the
# other.
#
# The two lines below agree on ALL FOUR key components (convention
# `pcre2`, kind `m`, no startpos, subject `"ab"`) and disagree only on
# the EXPECTATION, which is the one thing two `under` lines are never
# allowed to disagree about: a second correct answer per convention is
# the production's whole point, and two answers under ONE convention is
# a contradiction rather than a second answer. Class `schema-constraint`
# — the line attached correctly, `under` is legal here, and what failed
# is a DECLARED rule (`unique-by under-key`) over the scope.
#
# LEG A ONLY: `under`'s schema row reads `validated_by: pcrec`, and legs
# B and C treat every `under` line as a COUNTED, LABELLED SKIP (§2.17) —
# scoring a second correct answer is the consumer's act, not the
# harness's. Claiming three legs here would be §3.3's named failure.
pattern a|ab
under pcre2 m "ab" 0 1
under pcre2 m "ab" 0 2
m "ab" 0 1
